  aiOfflineDb: {"stainless":"For stainless steel (ISO M): Use AlTiN+Si nano-composite coating, 3-flute end mill with variable helix. Vc 60-100 m/min, high-pressure coolant ≥40 bar. Recommended: Seco JS554 or Sandvik CoroMill Plura 2P342.","aluminium":"For aluminium (ISO N): Use 2-3 flute DLC or polished AlTiN end mill. Vc 300-1000 m/min, MQL or compressed air. Recommended: ONMY 5040 or Gühring RF 100 Diver for slotting.","titanium":"For titanium Ti6Al4V (ISO S): Vc 40-60 m/min, small radial depth (≤20%D), trochoidal path, high-pressure coolant mandatory. AlTiN+Si coating. Recommended: Kennametal HARVI III or SGS Z-Carb.","hardened":"For hardened steel HRC45-65 (ISO H): CBN for turning (Sandvik CB7525 or Kennametal KB5640). AlCrN end mills for hard milling — Hermle or Mikron machine essential for rigidity. Vc 100-160 m/min milling, 150-300 m/min CBN turning.","inconel":"For Inconel 718 (ISO S): Vc 20-45 m/min, minimum radial engagement, sharp positive rake, ample coolant. Ceramic inserts for roughing at high speed. PVD TiAlN recommended. EMUGE ULTRA coating taps.","cast iron":"For cast iron (ISO K): Dry machining preferred. CVD Al2O3 coated inserts (Sandvik GC4325) or CBN for high speed. Short chips — ensure chip clearance. Vc 200-400 m/min turning.","tialn":"TiAlN (Titanium Aluminium Nitride): PVD coating, HV 2800, max 900°C. Industry workhorse for steel and stainless. Forms protective Al2O3 layer at high temp. Best for dry/MQL cutting.","alcr":"AlCrN (Aluminium Chromium Nitride): PVD, HV 3200, max 1100°C. Excellent oxidation resistance. Best choice for hardened steel milling. More stable than TiAlN at elevated temperatures.","dlc":"DLC (Diamond-Like Carbon): Extremely low friction µ=0.05, HV 5000. Only for non-ferrous (aluminium, copper, CFRP). Breaks down above 350°C — never use on steel. Mirror finish in aluminium.","cbn":"CBN (Cubic Boron Nitride): HV 4500, 2nd hardest material. ONLY for ferrous metals — reacts with aluminium. Hard turning HRC45-65 replacing grinding. Sandvik, Kennametal, Seco, Mitsubishi all offer CBN inserts.","chatter":"Troubleshooting chatter: 1) Reduce radial depth ae first. 2) Try variable-helix end mill (Sandvik CoroMill Plura). 3) Increase feed — light feed causes chatter. 4) Check spindle bearings and tool runout. 5) Anti-vibration boring bar for L/D>4. 6) Change spindle speed ±20%.","drill":"For general drilling: Solid carbide TiAlN drill (Gühring RT 100, Sandvik CoroDrill 460) for steel. Through-tool coolant above 3×D depth. 140° split point for self-centering. 9×D max without peck cycles.","vmc":"VMC (Vertical Machining Centre): Standard milling machine. Spindle vertical. Good for prismatic parts. Common brands: Haas VF-series (value), DMG Mori CMX (premium), Mazak VCN (mid-high). BT40 or HSK-A63 spindle.","sandvik":"Sandvik Coromant: World leader. CoroMill Plura end mills, CoroDrill 860 drills, GC4325/GC4315 turning grades. Excellent for production environments. Premium pricing. CoroPlus digital ecosystem. Website: sandvik.coromant.com","onmy":"ONMY Toolings (Changzhou Angmai): Chinese specialist founded 2014. Products: MUGEN-coated end mills (5010-8406), carbide drills (3310-3710), tungsten taps/thread mills (9100-9800), deburring tools (BS1010), Swiss collets for Citizen/Tsugami/Star/Tornos/Hanwha. Website: onmy-tools.com.","mugen":"MUGEN Coating (ONMY): Unlimited TiAlN PVD series. MUGEN Unlimited — highest performance, ∞ coating layers, max 1050°C, HV 3200. MUGEN Premium and MUGEN Micro for fine work. Best for steel, stainless, titanium, hardened steels to HRC 68."},
